{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791539041,"nonce":"FfZN3+M+uM4imcOloDhMiPJJnPs=","title":"The application preset promotes to LLVM at 250 interpreted calls/back-edges, only 2.5x its Cranelift threshold of 100. Ordinary short GUI interactions pay compiler and retained metadata costs before the extra throughput can amortise them.","message":"Raise only Application's LLVM threshold to 10,000. Keep its Cranelift threshold at 100 and keep LLVM available for sustained hot work. Align CLI help with the actual preset and document direct compiled calls not increasing the counters.\n\nAshui TreeMotion, macOS, rebuilt Ash, two sequential rounds in reversed order with identical bytecode/native libraries and the real interaction script:\n- old 250: physical footprint 216.20 / 195.45 MiB (mean 205.83), 39-41 LLVM installs\n- application 10,000: 198.89 / 170.66 MiB (mean 184.77), 5 LLVM installs\n- Cranelift only: 191.08 / 173.08 MiB (mean 182.08), 0 LLVM installs\n- animation frame work p95: old 1.2 / 1.5 ms; new 1.2 / 2.0 ms; Cranelift only 1.3 / 2.0 ms\n\nMean saving 21.06 MiB (10.2%). Absolute footprint varies with JIT/driver scheduling and collection timing; compare paired runs, not historical single samples. CLI ladder confirms auto tier0=100 tier1=10000, and explicit --opt-threshold 250 still works. Trace shows most warm UI functions remain in Cranelift.\n\nLocal diagnostic report in ashui: .ashui/memory-comparison/application-103849/report.json. Remaining runtime/renderer memory is investigated separately in ashui d701ddf and Ash f60b855 / 6fde0a9 / d0ca1c3.","files":null}]}